      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Recently we can use a new family of serological markers to objective myocardial damage with hig sensibility and specificity. One of these markers is T troponin (c-TNT). Some cocaine abusers have chest pain during drug consumption due to myocardial ischemia produced by the drug."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To study if in the chest pain appeared after cocaine consumption a c-TNT increased is objective, showing myocardial cellular damage."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
          "content": "We studied 65 patients; 35 cocaine abusers that were admitted into the emergency room for chest pain after cocaine consumption and 30 patients with no coronary chest pain. To all of them were determined c-TNT and CK."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "An increase in c-TNT or CK was not observed in both groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "We don't observe an increase in c-TNT in the group of cocaine abusers that evidence myocardial cellular damage."
        }
      ]},
